2026-07-04T22:33:17+0100 Zipper Range direct child locality under memory cap:
- Tightened `SpaceZipper.Range`, `LastRange`, and `DropLastRange` so direct `child(item)` no longer forces the whole selected child vector/map.
- `Range.child(item)` now performs a one-key ordered border walk and stops when the queried key is found, passed, or beyond the slice border.
- `LastRange.child(item)` and `DropLastRange.child(item)` now walk only the right border needed for that key, with per-key memoization for repeated descents.
- Added a regression proving `Range.child(a)` does not size an unrelated `b` sibling even when `b` lies inside the requested range window. This would have forced `selectedChildren` under the old implementation.
- This is an implementation-level Range expansion rather than a new law: it preserves the existing ordered range semantics while improving the zipper movement cost profile.

